> might under-estimate the total number of genes on which the effect of
> interest is significant.

Why do you think so?  The only disadvantage of keeping a non-significant term in the model is a
reduction in residual degrees of freedom, with some consequential loss of power, but this
disadvantage is mitigated by the empirical Bayes moderation process.

Perhaps someday someone will work out a model selection theory for massively parallel regression
situations like microarray experiments, but there isn't such a theory now.  It seems safer to me
to have the same model for every gene, keeping all the 'a priori' important predictors in the
model.

Gordon

