One more consideration: R and Bioconductor have pretty short release
cycles (a major release every 6 months, sometimes minor releases in
between), and for some of the frequently used packages, there have been
many more intermediate "development versions" that people wanted to use as
soon as they came out. Sometimes the updates were not backwards
