From jmacdon at med.umich.edu  Fri Jan 28 03:57:16 2005
From: jmacdon at med.umich.edu (James W. MacDonald)
Date: Fri Jan 28 03:57:26 2005
Subject: [BioC] Logged or unlogged data for multtest and limma?
In-Reply-To: <BAY101-F1849511ABE4BFDFD649529E8780@phx.gbl>
References: <BAY101-F1849511ABE4BFDFD649529E8780@phx.gbl>
Message-ID: <41F9AA0C.20006@med.umich.edu>

Ken Termiso wrote:
> Hi all,
> 
> As we all know, rma & gcrma return log2 values, while li-wong and mas5 
> results are unlogged. I'm pretty sure that limma wants logged data, but 
> how about multtest?

Although multtest uses a permuted null distribution and thus there is 
not necessarily an assumption of normally distributed (or at least 
roughly symmetrical) data, I think it is still prudent to log. This is 
because you are still using means, which are not robust to outliers.

> 
> Thanks in advance,
> Ken
